115:| US-01-BR-07 | Assessment: "The same application and the same build serve Colombia and Chile." Business context: "Each country has its own regulations, identity documents, currency, coverages and copy, so the content the app consumes changes by country." | One production build serves both countries. The supported countries are the published `country` entries in Strapi, loaded once per full page load (ADR-0001); no country code, country name or country list exists in front-end code. The country context selects which content is loaded; no country-specific branch, field list or copy exists in front-end code (wizard chrome copy excepted, US-01-Q-14; the complete list is §8.1). A country code that is not in the loaded list shows the unknown-country state and loads no form. If the country list cannot be loaded, the root chooser and the unknown-country page show a load error with "Reintentar", never "Este país no está disponible." (ADR-0001). Data entered in one country context is never shown in the other (US-01-Q-02). | US-01-AC-01, US-01-AC-17, US-01-AC-22 |
499:    | /          | the country chooser with the links "Colombia" and "Chile" |
769:| US-01-Q-01 | **[Blocks HC1] [ADR]** "Open the application in the context of a country": how is the country resolved (URL path, query parameter, subdomain, selector, browser locale)? What happens with no country or an unsupported one? | AC-01, AC-17 and every e2e test depend on it. The same build must serve both countries (Assessment). | Decided by the multi-country ADR. Proposal to evaluate: a country segment in the URL (`/co/…`, `/cl/…`), so it can be deep-linked, bookmarked and tested. The root address shows a country chooser (links "Colombia", "Chile"). An unsupported code shows "Este país no está disponible." with the same links (AC-17). No detection from IP or browser locale. | Decided by the ADR. The proposal (/co, /cl, chooser at the root, message "Este país no está disponible.") is the starting point. — Felipe Sabogal, 2026-11-20 (HC1) |
796:| US-01-Q-28 | (new in v0.3, a consequence of ADR-0001) The country list is now content loaded from Strapi, so the root chooser and the unknown-country page have a loading state and a load-error state (§8, AC-17). ADR-0001 leaves their copy to the spec. "No pudimos cargar el formulario. Intenta de nuevo." is form-specific. What copy do they show? | Without it the developer invents end-user copy, or reuses the form message on a page that has no form. A wrong "Este país no está disponible." must never stand in for a load failure (ADR-0001). | Code-owned chrome copy, Spanish, the same for both countries, added to the US-01-Q-14 list: load error "No pudimos cargar la lista de países. Intenta de nuevo." with the existing "Reintentar"; loading "Cargando…". Same rules as the step 1 load states: 10 s timeout (US-01-Q-17), no automatic retries, error in `role="alert"`, focus on "Reintentar". | OK (proposed default accepted). — Felipe Sabogal, 2026-11-20 (HC1 round 3) |
1034:| Country list loading | Root chooser or unknown-country page, country list request in flight (ADR-0001) | "Cargando…" (proposed, US-01-Q-28); no country link, no "Este país no está disponible." | Container has `aria-busy="true"`; the loading text is in a polite live region |
1035:| Country list unavailable | Root chooser or unknown-country page; the country list request times out (10 s) or fails (ADR-0001) | "No pudimos cargar la lista de países. Intenta de nuevo." (proposed, US-01-Q-28) and "Reintentar"; no country link, and never "Este país no está disponible." (AC-17) | Message in `role="alert"`; focus moves to "Reintentar" |
1036:| Country chooser (v0.4) | Root address `/`, country list loaded (ADR-0001, US-01-Q-01) | Heading "Elige tu país" and a link to each published country (seed: "Colombia", "Chile") | The heading is the page's main heading; links are reachable by Tab |
